& [CoreConclusion] is a permission-bounded proactive desktop operator shell
  + the new multi-target language naturally supports a human-facing assistant through SOP-T tool projections and SOP-W workflow programs
  + Cantor can recognize a task, retrieve its semantic and operational contracts, form a plan, request exact authority, invoke tools, monitor effects, and preserve reentry
  + an LLM may interpret requests, explain opportunities, propose plans, and articulate results while Cantor owns task state, capability, effect gates, and proof
  + proactive assistance means initiating a proposal from an authorized trigger, not silently initiating an effect
  + the shell is an application profile over SOP and Cantor rather than a new language-core primitive
  = concise: build super-Clippy as a transparent semantic task manager with tools, memory, consent, and recovery

& [ApplicationIdentity] is the Cantor Operator Shell candidate
  + [user_role] is principal, purpose source, preference owner, authority grantor, and final recipient
  + [shell_role] is contextual interface, task ledger, proposal surface, notification broker, and reentry coordinator
  + [Cantor_role] is semantic resolution, SOP retrieval, contract compilation, planning gates, capability mediation, trace, and proof
  + [model_role] is interpretation, candidate generation, explanation, drafting, and conversational articulation
  + [tool_adapter_role] is typed observation or operation against one declared computer surface
  + [effect_broker_role] is sole committer of authorized external or persistent changes
  = must: preserve identity and attribution for every participant, tool, task, and effect

& [OperatorCycle] is the complete assistance loop
  * receive an explicit request or admitted proactive trigger
  * bind current user, device, session, foreground purpose, and privacy scope
  * observe only the authorized minimum context
  * resolve the possible task against signed SOP identities, operations, capabilities, preferences, and prior task state
  * distinguish fact, inference, opportunity, reminder, request, and fault
  * form a TaskContract and one or more bounded CandidatePlans
  * present purpose, evidence, steps, effects, risk, reversibility, uncertainty, and required consent
  * obtain or verify an exact current capability grant
  * execute through typed tools while monitoring preconditions and state versions
  * pause, replan, compensate, or stop on material divergence
  * report results, effects, residual work, proof, and recovery instructions
  * update the task ledger, narrative, preferences only when authorized, and exact reentry state

& [TaskContract] makes a conversational request executable
  + [task_uuid] is stable task identity
  + [principal] is the requesting and authorizing user identity
  + [purpose] is the invariant intended outcome
  + [trigger] is explicit request, schedule, event, monitored condition, resumed task, or bounded opportunity rule
  + [inputs] is user-provided and separately observed context
  + [assumptions] is explicit conditional operating material
  + [preconditions] is required entry truth
  + [plan_space] is permitted operations and alternatives
  + [capabilities] is exact tools, resources, scopes, limits, and expiry
  + [effects] is proposed persistent, external, communicative, privileged, or destructive change
  + [approval_policy] is which effects require preview, confirmation, step-up, or are prohibited
  + [invariants] is identity, privacy, security, honesty, preservation, and user-intention conditions
  + [completion] is observable success evidence
  + [faults] is typed failure, divergence, ambiguity, denial, timeout, interruption, and unavailable capability
  + [recovery] is retry, rollback, compensate, quarantine, manual handoff, or preserved reentry
  + [termination] is complete, yielded, suspended, blocked, cancelled, faulted, or budget exhausted

& [TaskStateMachine] keeps initiative inspectable
  + [Dormant] has no active observation beyond declared listeners
  + [Attending] receives one authorized request or trigger and forms bounded context
  + [Proposing] resolves purpose and prepares non-effecting options
  + [AwaitingConsent] exposes material effects and waits without treating silence as approval
  + [Executing] invokes only granted capabilities under current preconditions
  + [Monitoring] compares expected and observed effects and detects divergence
  + [Yielded] preserves exact continuation while returning control to the user
  + [Suspended] stops work because context, authority, availability, or relevance changed
  + [Recovering] applies an authorized rollback or compensation contract
  + [Completed] proves the completion contract and reports residuals
  + [Faulted] preserves state and recovery instructions without concealing partial effects
  = must: make every transition visible and attributable

& [ProactiveAssistanceBoundary] preserves usefulness without nuisance or surveillance
  + [eligible_trigger] is an explicit schedule, subscribed event, user-declared recurring purpose, resumed incomplete task, or locally detected condition inside an authorized observation scope
  + [proposal_only_default] may surface a concise suggestion or draft without invoking effecting tools
  + [pertinence_gate] checks current purpose, confidence, evidence, urgency, interruption cost, recent dismissal, and duplicate state
  + [interruption_budget] limits frequency, modality, priority, quiet hours, and escalation
  + [dismissal_memory] suppresses repeated proposals under an explicit retention policy
  + [snooze] preserves the task and exact wake condition without claiming future authority
  = must: let the user inspect, mute, scope, pause, or disable every trigger class
  - never: infer consent from engagement, non-response, prior unrelated approval, or model confidence

& [ContextAndPrivacyBoundary] defines what the shell may know
  + [foreground_context] is user-supplied request, selected files, selected applications, and explicitly shared screen or state
  + [subscribed_context] is named events and resources admitted under one listener contract
  + [sensitive_context] includes credentials, private messages, clipboard, microphone, camera, health, finance, location, and protected files
  + [context_snapshot] records source, collection method, purpose, scope, time, expiry, sensitivity, and redaction
  + [local_first] keeps semantic retrieval, task ledger, and sensitive filtering local unless an exact provider disclosure contract says otherwise
  = must: minimize collection and projection to what the active TaskContract requires
  = must: distinguish local observation from content transmitted to a model or external tool
  - never: enable ambient screen, audio, clipboard, message, or filesystem monitoring by implication

& [ConsentAndEffectClasses] establishes graduated computer-operation authority
  + [E0_observe] is bounded read-only inspection with disclosed scope
  + [E1_prepare] is draft, preview, simulate, calculate, or stage without persistent target change
  + [E2_reversible_local] is a bounded local change with proved rollback and no external communication
  + [E3_persistent_or_external] is durable application state, communication, publication, scheduling, or network-side mutation
  + [E4_privileged_or_high_consequence] is credentials, system configuration, security boundary, destructive action, financial commitment, or broad irreversible effect
  + [approval] is profile-specific and may require per-plan, per-step, destination-bound, content-bound, or fresh step-up consent
  = must: begin with E0 and E1 only for the first profile
  = must: revalidate authority immediately before every effect
  - never: let a broad natural-language request become an unbounded capability token

& [CapabilityBroker] separates knowing how from permission to act
  + [discovery] resolves signed capability descriptors pertinent to one task
  + [availability] confirms current application, device, account, session, and adapter state
  + [grant] binds principal, task, operation, resource, limits, effect class, expiry, nonce, and revocation
  + [invocation] requires current task state, plan step, preconditions, adapter identity, and grant
  + [result] records observation, proposed or committed effects, tool evidence, faults, and state version
  = must: keep tool discovery, loading, invocation, authorization, and effect commitment separate

& [TaskLedgerAndMemory] is inspectable continuity rather than hidden persona
  + [task_record] preserves purpose, state, plan, decisions, effects, proof, residuals, and reentry
  + [preference_contract] records explicit assistance style, notification, privacy, provider, tool, approval, and retention choices
  + [routine] is a user-admitted reusable TaskContract template with version, trigger, inputs, limits, and approval profile
  + [working_context] is short-lived task state with expiry
  + [semantic_memory] is signed SOP and user-authored stable definitions
  + [narrative_memory] is attributed history used only when pertinent to the current subject
  = must: expose why a memory influenced a proposal or plan
  = must: allow correction, deletion, expiry, export, and disablement under applicable authority
  - never: turn inferred behavior into a durable preference without disclosure and admission

& [FacultyOperation] coordinates the desktop agent
  + [Observer] identifies trigger, context, task state, and material changes
  + [Honesty] checks request interpretation, application and resource identity, claims, evidence, uncertainty, and result correspondence
  + [Security] checks principal, capability, scope, sensitivity, effects, containment, reversibility, and disclosure
  + [Scribe] records TaskContract, plan, source, approvals, tool calls, effects, results, and reentry
  + [Refiner] makes the proposal minimal, comprehensible, non-duplicative, and semantically sufficient
  + [Weaver] binds applications, files, services, tools, data, and SOP routines into compatible candidate actions
  + [Planner] orders steps, approvals, checkpoints, monitoring, fallback, compensation, and completion
  = must: require Observer disposition before execution and after effect observation

& [UserExperiencePrinciples] preserve the useful part of Clippy
  + [small_surface] is one concise card showing perceived task, reason, proposed help, material effects, and choices
  + [progressive_disclosure] opens exact plan, sources, permissions, memory, and proof on demand
  + [direct_control] is do, preview, edit plan, snooze, dismiss, mute trigger, stop, undo, and explain
  + [quiet_progress] reports only meaningful checkpoints during execution
  + [truthful_status] distinguishes preparing, waiting, executing, monitoring, blocked, and complete
  + [reentry] shows exactly what remains and what changed when the user returns
  = should: feel like a capable secretary and task manager rather than an attention-seeking mascot

& [MultiTargetExecution] applies the new SOP purpose
  + [SOP_X] executes task state, contracts, approvals, deterministic transforms, tool schemas, gates, trace, and recovery
  + [SOP_N] recognizes candidate tasks, retrieves routines, ranks plans, predicts faults, and drafts explanations
  + [SOP_H] lets learned proposals enter exact validation and capability mediation before computer effects
  + [SOP_T] projects minimum typed tools and results
  + [SOP_W] projects task workflows, faculty programs, checkpoints, and compensation
  + [SOP_I] projects cards, plans, permission prompts, diagnostics, and proof for the user

& [ExistingSupport] is substantial but not desktop-effect ready
  + [available] is semantic query, signed packages, CLI, MCP, resident service, lifecycle supervision, task-like work packets, faculty cycle, narrative, tool discovery, bounded candidate mutation, and embodied-agent effect concepts
  + [missing] is desktop observation API, application identity registry, desktop capability broker, effect broker, consent UI, trigger manager, task ledger schema, undo integration, and sandboxed desktop fixture
  + [current_write_boundary] existing workspace mutation authority is narrow and must not be generalized into arbitrary desktop operation
  = conclusion: reuse semantic and governance substrate while sourcing every physical desktop capability separately

& [FirstProof] is a simulated then disposable desktop task
  + [simulation] uses a deterministic fake desktop containing test applications, documents, events, permissions, and effects
  + [request] asks the shell to recognize and prepare one bounded organization or work-session task
  + [proposal] shows exact purpose, plan, affected test resources, effect class, rollback, and consent
  + [fault] includes stale observation, wrong application identity, changed target, revoked grant, repeated notification, denied consent, and partial tool failure
  + [execution] is E0 and E1 only in the first proof, with no real persistent desktop effect
  + [second_gate] permits one operator-explicit E2 action only inside a disposable contained fixture with byte-proved rollback
  + [acceptance] is no ambient observation, no unauthorized effect, exact replay, useful proposal, visible stop, and complete reentry

& [FaultSet] is mandatory
  + [ambient_authority] treats resident operation as permission to observe or act
  + [intent_overreach] expands a broad goal into undeclared subgoals or effects
  + [notification_pressure] repeatedly interrupts, manipulates, or infers approval from fatigue
  + [context_leak] transmits local sensitive context beyond the declared provider boundary
  + [stale_desktop] acts on a window, file, account, or selection that changed after planning
  + [capability_confusion] treats tool availability as invocation or effect authority
  + [partial_effect_concealment] reports failure without disclosing changes already committed
  + [memory_profile_laundering] turns inference into durable user preference
  + [undo_claim] promises reversal without a proved compensation path
  + [agent_personification] lets friendly presentation obscure model uncertainty, tool identity, or responsible principal

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is COS-001 through COS-030
  + [COS-001] define Cantor Operator Shell as an application profile rather than language core
  + [COS-002] implement observe, recognize, propose, consent, execute, monitor, recover, report, and reenter as explicit stages
  + [COS-003] define one complete TaskContract and inspectable task state machine
  + [COS-004] distinguish explicit requests from admitted proactive triggers
  + [COS-005] make proactive behavior proposal-only by default
  + [COS-006] enforce pertinence, interruption budgets, quiet hours, dismissal memory, and trigger control
  + [COS-007] minimize context collection and disclose model or tool projection
  + [COS-008] prohibit implicit ambient screen, audio, clipboard, message, and filesystem monitoring
  + [COS-009] classify observation, preparation, reversible local, persistent external, and privileged effects
  + [COS-010] begin the first profile with E0 and E1 only
  + [COS-011] bind every capability grant to principal, task, operation, resource, effect, limit, and expiry
  + [COS-012] separate discovery, availability, loading, invocation, authorization, and commitment
  + [COS-013] revalidate target identity, state, preconditions, and authority before effects
  + [COS-014] preserve partial effects, faults, rollback, compensation, and manual recovery honestly
  + [COS-015] make task, preference, routine, working, semantic, and narrative memory separately inspectable
  + [COS-016] forbid undisclosed inferred durable preferences
  + [COS-017] let the user correct, expire, delete, export, mute, pause, and disable applicable state
  + [COS-018] compile materially pertinent faculty programs into every effecting workflow
  + [COS-019] provide concise cards plus progressive plan, authority, source, memory, and proof inspection
  + [COS-020] expose preview, plan edit, snooze, dismiss, mute, stop, undo, and explain controls where truthful
  + [COS-021] project task execution through SOP-X, SOP-N, SOP-H, SOP-T, SOP-W, and SOP-I
  + [COS-022] keep model output advisory and effect commitment deterministic and capability-bound
  + [COS-023] preserve exact reentry and user-visible residual work
  + [COS-024] build application, account, window, resource, tool, and adapter identity registries before real desktop action
  + [COS-025] source each physical desktop observation and effect capability separately
  + [COS-026] prove a deterministic fake-desktop E0 and E1 fixture first
  + [COS-027] gate one E2 proof inside an operator-explicit disposable contained fixture
  + [COS-028] require zero ambient observation, unauthorized effect, context leak, stale effect, and concealed partial effect
  + [COS-029] measure usefulness, interruption cost, plan correction, consent burden, latency, recovery, and proof completeness
  + [COS-030] preserve current read-only, workspace-write, service, and operator boundaries until separate activation authority exists

& [Decision] is preserve the Operator Shell candidate behind application-profile SJS
  + [architecture_fit] is high with SOP-T, SOP-W, SOP-I, TaskContract, faculties, narrative, tool discovery, and embodied effect mediation
  + [canonical_authority] existing language, runtime, tool, capability, effect, service, and workspace specifications remain authoritative
  + [new_canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [desktop_observation_authority] is absent
  + [desktop_effect_authority] is absent
  + [schedule_effect] add COS-SJS-01 after SMTC language-purpose reconciliation and before any real desktop listener or effect adapter
  + [first_candidate_after_authority] is deterministic fake-desktop E0 and E1 assistance only
  + [reasoning_depth] application architecture, privacy, capability, effect, recovery, and UX reconciliation require deeper reasoning; a closed fake-desktop fixture becomes Spark-suitable after signed activation authority
